cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below."
title: "Kaczmarz-LP: benchmark of sparse LP solvers versus classical graph algorithms (time and peak memory)"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Russo
    given-names: "Luís M. S."
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1966-1808"
    affiliation: "INESC-ID, Instituto Superior Técnico, Universidade de Lisboa"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/LuisRusso-INESC-ID/Kaczmarz-LP"
abstract: >-
  Benchmark harness, instance generators, raw results and analysis scripts comparing general
  sparse LP solvers (HiGHS, Clp, GLPK, OR-Tools GLOP and PDLP, Gurobi as a commercial reference,
  and own PDHG and Kaczmarz-style
  prototypes) with classical combinatorial codes (Dijkstra, push-relabel including HIPR,
  pseudoflow, Boykov-Kolmogorov, network simplex, Garg-Könemann) on shortest paths, maximum flow and maximum concurrent flow, measuring solve
  time and net peak memory per arc, on synthetic families and the 9th DIMACS USA road network.
keywords:
  - linear programming
  - benchmark
  - peak memory
  - shortest paths
  - maximum flow
  - multicommodity flow
  - PDLP
  - Kaczmarz method
